simrad.AR: Implementation of a radar emulator in WRF

L. Fita, V. Galligani (CIMA-IFAECI), Aregntina

This effort is absolutely in shoulders of giants and is based in multiple different works:

 - Bessel, F. W., (1826) On the computation of geographical longitude and latitude from geodetic measurements, Astronomische Nachrichten (Astronomical Notes), Band 4, No. 86, Spalten 241-254, Altona 1826
 - Leinonen, J., High-level interface to T-matrix scattering calculations: architecture, capabilities and limitations, Opt. Express, vol. 22, issue 2, 1655-1660 (2014), doi: 10.1364/OE.22.001655.
 - Mishchenko, M. I. and L. D. Travis, T-matrix computations of light scattering by large spheroidal particles, Opt. Commun., vol. 109, 16-21 (1994)
 - Mishchenko, M. I., L. D. Travis, and A. Macke, Scattering of light by polydisperse, randomly oriented, finite circular cylinders, Appl. Opt., vol. 35, 4927-4940 (1996)
 - Vincenty, T., (1975) Direct and inverse solutions on the ellipsoid with application of nested equations, Survey Review, Vol. 23, No. 176, pp. 88-93.
 - Vincenty, T., (1976) Correspondence: solutions of geodesics, survey Review, Vol. 23, No. 180, p. 294.
 - Wielaard, D. J., M. I. Mishchenko, A. Macke, and B. E. Carlson, Improved T-matrix computations for large, nonabsorbing and weakly absorbing nonspherical particles and comparison with geometrical optics approximation, Appl. Opt., vol. 36, 4305-4313 (1997)


There is a prototype off-line working version available from CIMA's GIT repository, from which the code is based on:
https://git.cima.fcen.uba.ar/lluis.fita/simradar/-/wikis/home

This code is available from Lluis Fita's WRF fork (git@github.com:LluisFB/WRF.git) in branch 'simradAR'

== Usage ==
A new section into the WRF's namelist calles 'simradar' has to be set up

=== namelist ===
simradar&
/

| type     | name                | default value       | description                                                        | units |
| ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- |
|integer   | nradar              | 1                   | amount of surface radar                                            | # |
|integer   | e_dist              | 800                 | radar grid points along the radii                                  | # |
|integer   | e_angle             | 376                 | radar amount of horizontal angles                                  | # |
|integer   | e_azimuth           | 15                  | radar amount of azimuths                                           | # |
|integer   | ngrid_radar         | 1500                | maximum amount of radar cells into a given WRF grid point          | # |
|integer   | ngrid3_radar        | 25000               | maximum amount of vertical radar cells into a given WRF grid point | # | 
|integer   | nradar_ngrid        | 30000               | nradar*ngrid_radar                                                 | # |
|integer   | nradar_ngrid_coord2 | 60000               | nradar_ngrid_coord2                                                | # |
|integer   | nradar_coord2       | 40                  | nradar*coord2                                                      | # |
|integer   | nradar_coord4       | 160                 | nradar*coord4                                                      | # |
|integer   | ngrid_coord2        | 60000               | ngrid_radar*coord2                                                 | # |
|integer   | nradar_azimuth      | 300                 | nradar*e_azimuth                                                   | # |
|integer   | nradar_dist         | 1600                | nradar*e_dist                                                      | # |
|integer   | Nbands              | 3                   | amount of radar bands                                              | # |
|integer   | Nluticebins         | 200                 | amount of ice bins for LUT interpolations                          | # |
|integer   | Nlutqxbins          | 50000               | amount of water species bins for LUT interpolations                | # |
|integer   | Nlutlevs            | 15                  | amount of azimuths for LUT interpolations                          | # |
|character | radar_name          | '-'                 | name of the radar [one per radar]                                  | - |
|real      | radar_clon          | 0.0                 | longitude of the location of the radar    [one per radar]          | degree_east  |
|real      | radar_clat          | 0.0                 | latitude of the location of the radar [one per radar]              | degree_north |
|real      | radar_chgt          | 0.0                 | height of the location of the radar  [one per radar]               | m |
|character | radar_band          | '-'                 | band of the radar: 'c', 's', or 'x'  [one per radar]               | - |
|integer   | radar_scan          | 1                   | type of scan 1:             [one per radar]                        | - |
|real      | radar_distmax       | 250.                | maximum distance from radar [one per radar]                        | km |
|real      | radar_hgtmax        | 20.                 | maximum height from radar  [one per radar]                         | km |
|integer   | em_ray              | 1                   | type of propagation of em ray. 1: 4/3 Ref [one per radar]          | - |
|real      | radards             | 250.                | nominal horizontal resolution of radar values [one per radar]      | m |
|integer   | radinterp           | 1                   | method of interpolation to the radar space (1: inverted distance weighted) | - |
|real      | radii_dist          | 15.                 | radii at which arc resolution is the same as minimum radards       | km |
|integer   | eloption            | 1                   | Ellipsoide                                                         | - |
|real      | missing_value       | 1.e20               | missing value                                                      | - |
|integer   | doppler_scheme      | 1                   | method to compute the doppler velocities                           | - |
|integer   | timedbg             | 720                 | frecuency of time-debugging                                        | minute |
|real      | londbg              | -999.               | longitude of grid-point debugging (-999., not used)                | degree_east  |
|real      | latdbg              | -999.               | latitude of grid-point debugging (-999., not used)                 | degree_north |
|character | lutfilen            | TMATRIX_WRF_WSM6.nc | name of the netCDF file with the T-Matrix lool-up-tables           | - |
|real      | q_rain_min          | 1e-7                | minimum rain mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1" |
|real      | q_rain_max          | 0.02                | maximum rain mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1 |
|real      | qn_rain_min         | 1e-8                | minimum amount of nuclii for rain to consider                      | # |
|real      | qn_rain_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for rain to consider                      | # |
|real      | q_snow_min          | 1e-7                | minimum snow mixing ratio to consider                              | kgkg-1 |
|real      | q_snow_max          | 0.018               | maximum snow mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | qn_snow_min         | 1e-7                | minimum amount of nuclii for snow to consider"                     | # |
|real      | qn_snow_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for snow to consider"                     | # |
|real      | q_grau_min          | 1e-7                | minimum grau mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | q_grau_max          | 0.018               | maximum grau mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | qn_grau_min         | 1E-7                | minimum amount of nuclii for grau to consider"                     | # |
|real      | qn_grau_max         | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for grau to consider"                     | # |
|real      | q_ice_min           | 1e-7                | minimum cloud ice mixing ratio to consider"                        | kgkg-1 |
|real      | q_ice_max           | 0.001               | maximum cloud ice mixing ratio to consider"                        | kgkg-1 |
|real      | qn_ice_min          | 1e-8                | minimum amount of nuclii for cloud ice to consider"                | # |
|real      | qn_ice_max          | 2.6e6               | maximum amount of nuclii for cloud ice to consider"                | # |
|real      | q_hail_min          | -9999.              | minimum hail mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | q_hail_max          | -9999.              | maximum hail mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | qn_hail_min         | -9999.              | minimum amount of nuclii for hail to consider"                     | # |
|real      | qn_hail_max         | -9999.              | maximum amount of nuclii for hail to consider"                     | # |
|real      | q_clou_min          | 1e-10               | minimum clou mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|real      | q_clou_max          | 0.013               | maximum clou mixing ratio to consider"                             | kgkg-1 |
|integer   | dim_ice             | 200                 | dimension for ice bins"                                            | - |
|integer   | Nqxbins             | 50000               | dimension for water species bins"                                  | - |


== Installation ==

1.- Get the repository from a $WORKDIR
git clone git@github.com:LluisFB/WRF.git

2.- getting submoules
git submodule update --init --recursive

3.- Switching to the simrad.AR branch
git checkout simradAR

4.- Preparing installation (remember to define WRFIO_NCD_LARGE_FILE_SUPPORT=1 and NETCDF)
./configure

5.- Editing configure.wrf to add -DSIMRADAR pre-compilation flag
cp configure.wrf configure.simradAR.orig
cp configure.wrf configure.simradAR.wrf
vim configure.simradAR.wrf
diff configure.wrf.orig configure.simradAR.wrf
216c216
<                        \
---
>                       -DSIMRADAR \
cp configure.simradAR.wrf configure.wrf

6.- Compile as usual
./compile em_real >& compile.log



